From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 09:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Upload visible rows from padded live frames

CPU-backed Media Engine samples can contain codec or allocator padding beyond
the visible texture dimensions.  The render transfer path required the sample
length to exactly match the visible byte count, silently skipped the upload
when a padded sample was larger, and nevertheless returned success after
drawing the unchanged intermediate texture.

Accept buffers containing at least the visible rows and retain the visible
row pitch passed to UpdateSubresource.  Emit a bounded live-stream diagnostic
for the source and required sizes while validating the winedmo HLS path.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -2935,6 +2935,7 @@ static HRESULT get_d3d11_resource_from_sample(IMFSample *sample, ID3D11Texture2D
 
 static void media_engine_update_d3d11_frame_surface(ID3D11DeviceContext *context, struct media_engine *engine)
 {
+    static LONG live_upload_diagnostic_count;
     D3D11_TEXTURE2D_DESC surface_desc;
     D3D11_TEXTURE2D_DESC src_desc;
     IMFMediaBuffer *media_buffer;
@@ -2979,10 +2980,19 @@ static void media_engine_update_d3d11_frame_surface(ID3D11DeviceContext *context
     if (FAILED(hr) && SUCCEEDED(IMFSample_ConvertToContiguousBuffer(sample, &media_buffer)))
     {
         BYTE *buffer;
+        DWORD expected_size;
         DWORD buffer_size;
         if (SUCCEEDED(IMFMediaBuffer_Lock(media_buffer, &buffer, NULL, &buffer_size)))
         {
-            if (buffer_size == surface_desc.Width * surface_desc.Height)
+            LONG diagnostic_id = 0;
+
+            expected_size = surface_desc.Width * surface_desc.Height;
+            if (isinf(engine->duration))
+                diagnostic_id = InterlockedIncrement(&live_upload_diagnostic_count);
+            if (diagnostic_id && diagnostic_id <= 16)
+                WARN("live-upload diagnostic %ld: buffer %lu bytes, visible %lu bytes, pitch %u, height %u.\n",
+                        diagnostic_id, buffer_size, expected_size, surface_desc.Width, surface_desc.Height);
+            if (buffer_size >= expected_size)
             {
                 ID3D11DeviceContext_UpdateSubresource(context, (ID3D11Resource *)engine->video_frame.d3d11.source,
                         0, NULL, buffer, surface_desc.Width, 0);
-- 
